Question_Text:
47. Let f(x) = x² and g(x) = sinx for all x∈ R. Then the set of all x satisfying (f◦g◦g◦f)(x) = (g◦g◦f)(x), where (f◦g)(x) = f(g(x)), is
(A) ±√nπ, n∈ {0, 1, 2,...}
(B) ±√nπ, n∈ {1, 2,...}
(C) π/2 + 2nπ, n∈ {..., -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, ...}
(D) 2nπ, n∈ {..., -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, ...}

A linear octasaccharide (molar mass = 1024 g mol⁻¹) on complete hydrolysis produces three monosaccharides: ribose, 2-deoxyribose and glucose. The amount of 2-deoxyribose formed is 58.26% (w/w) of the total amount of the monosaccharides produced in the hydrolyzed products. The number of ribose unit(s) present in one molecule of octasaccharide is
Use: Molar mass (in g mol⁻¹): ribose = 150, 2-deoxyribose = 134, glucose = 180;
Atomic mass (in amu): H = 1, O = 16
